{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"pilot","tool":"container_exec","arguments":{"command":"cat '/work/artifacts/phase2_prompt_packs/prob_13_9/task.json'","timeout_seconds":30},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.20300000000861473, \"stdout\": \"{\\n  \\\"block_id\\\": \\\"prob_13_9\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"Problem\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Problem 13.9\\\",\\n  \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\\textbf{13.9.} Suppose (X n)n\\\\\\\\geq0 is a sequence of random variables defined on a probability\\\\n\\\\nspace (we take X 0 = 0 as the initial rv.)For n \\\\\\\\geq 1, let\\\\n\\\\nYn \\\\\\\\coloneqqX n -E [Xn\\\\\\\\vertX0,X 1,...,X n- 1].\\\\n\\\\nThe random variable Y n can be interpreted as the new information contained in X n\\\\n\\\\nrelative to the information contained in the past X 0,...,X n- 1Let Sn denote the\\\\n\\\\npartial sum S n \\\\\\\\coloneqqY 1 +Y 2 +\\\\\\\\cdot\\\\\\\\cdot\\\\\\\\cdot+ Yn for n \\\\\\\\geq 1 and S 0 = 0. Show that (S n)n\\\\\\\\geq0 is a\\\\n\\\\nmartingale relative to the filtration (\\\\\\\\sigma(X 1,X 2,...,X n))n\\\\\\\\geq0.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"source_plan\\\": \\\"experiment_targets\\\",\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": [],\\n  \\\"soft_imports\\\": [],\\n  \\\"soft_imports_confirmed_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-10T15:10:29.795043+00:00\\\",\\n  \\\"final_import_union\\\": []\\n}\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"stdout_truncated\": false, \"stderr_truncated\": false, \"raw_stdout\": {\"bytes\": 849, \"sha256\": \"216e6c5a254e4cbe0c517c85135dd5fff1f877a374e1f4de651f2d834586ab15\"}, \"raw_stderr\": {\"bytes\": 0, \"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\"}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
